    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Use number of and fewer with countable nouns]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45498</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45498"/>
        <updated>2026-09-04T07:11:57.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Uses "number of" and "fewer" rather than "amount of" and "less" with countable nouns, in 29 places.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">"Amount" and "less" go with mass nouns; countable nouns take "number" and "fewer". The repository already follows this almost everywhere, so these are outliers rather than a house style: "number of bytes" appears 156 times against 5 of "amount of bytes", "number of characters" 121 against 2, and "fewer" appears 164 times.</p>
<p dir="auto">The changes include "the amount of bytes that get downloaded", "Removes the specified amount of characters" on <code class="notranslate">CharacterData</code>, "the amount of rows in the collection" on <code class="notranslate">HTMLTableSectionElement</code>, "Returns the amount of objects in the map" on <code class="notranslate">NamedNodeMap</code>, "The amount of pixels to move the window", "an unreasonable amount of requests" on the two <code class="notranslate">XRSession</code> hit-test methods, and the three "Count the amount of … zeros" entries on the WebAssembly numeric reference.</p>
<p dir="auto">Also "kanban, which has less rules than scrum", and "If there are less values than glyphs" on the SVG <code class="notranslate">dx</code> and <code class="notranslate">dy</code> attribute pages.</p>
<p dir="auto">The hyphenated compound "extension-less requests" is left alone, since "less" there is a suffix rather than a quantifier.</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>husamemadH</name>
            <email>husamemadH@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/husamemadH</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-09-04T07:09:56.000Z</published>
